{number: 97}
{title: It is Well with My Soul}
{key: Db}

{start_of_verse: 1}
When [Db] peace like a river at-[Gb] tendeth my [Db] way,
When [Bbm] sorrows like [Eb7] sea billows [Ab7] roll;
What-[Db] ever my [Gb] lot, Thou hast [Eb7] taught me to [Ab7] say,
It is [Db] well, it is [Gb] well [Ab7] with my [Db] soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
It is [Db] well with my [Ab7] soul,
It is [Db] well, it is [Gb] well [Ab7] with my [Db] soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Though [Db] Satan should buffet, though [Gb] trials should [Db] come,
Let [Bbm] this blest as-[Eb7] surance con-[Ab7] trol,
That [Db] Christ has re-[Gb] garded my [Eb7] helpless es-[Ab7] tate,
And hath [Db] shed His own [Gb] blood [Ab7] for my [Db] soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
My [Db] sin, oh, the bliss of this [Gb] glorious [Db] thought!
My [Bbm] sin, not in [Eb7] part but the [Ab7] whole,
Is [Db] nailed to the [Gb] cross, and I [Eb7] bear it no [Ab7] more,
Praise the [Db] Lord, praise the [Gb] Lord, [Ab7] O my [Db] soul!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And [Db] Lord, haste the day when my [Gb] faith shall be [Db] sight,
The [Bbm] clouds be rolled [Eb7] back as a [Ab7] scroll;
The [Db] trump shall re-[Gb] sound, and the [Eb7] Lord shall de-[Ab7] scend,
